There you go. Good boy. Obey me.

258
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:54,125
Remember that I'm your master.

259
00:14:54,220 --> 00:14:55,926
Quest, I've told you to wait.

260
00:14:57,020 --> 00:14:59,785
You and I have so much
catching up to do first.

261
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:01,857
There was that one time.

262
00:15:01,940 --> 00:15:02,770
Remember?

263
00:15:03,380 --> 00:15:05,640
Yes, it was four years ago.

264
00:15:12,260 --> 00:15:13,560
Okay. Sure, okay.

265
00:15:13,700 --> 00:15:14,897
I wanted you to eat it now.

266
00:15:14,980 --> 00:15:15,810
Good boy.

267
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:19,000
Yeah, he's not listening
to a word you say.

268
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:25,400
Smiley ate it!

269
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:28,700
Swallowed the candy hole! It's happening!

270
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:31,357
Good boy, Smiley!

271
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:32,660
Now be reborn!

272
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:43,940
Show them all of your power!

273
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:50,820
What kind of ugly baby is
it going to be reborn as?

274
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,941
The most powerful weapon
of mass destruction ever.

275
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:56,200
Man, that is one big frog.

276
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:08,637
Yo, crap, it's making
all sorts of bad noises.

277
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:09,550
What's it doing?

278
00:16:09,633 --> 00:16:10,463
I don't want to laugh.

279
00:16:10,546 --> 00:16:12,437
Neither do I, but I
know it's something bad.

280
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:16,237
We just got to keep running until we
get to the lab like a master said.

281
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:19,057
Dammit, why'd that stupid
sled have to go and break?

282
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:20,160
It's not fair!

283
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:21,940
Please help us, master!

284
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:25,697
I got a bad feeling about
the way that thing's acting.

285
00:16:25,780 --> 00:16:28,617
They're up that giant candy,
giving a spot of indigestion.

286
00:16:28,700 --> 00:16:30,171
Quit speculating and run!

287
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:32,837
Have you not noticed the frantic
flight of the island's soldiers?

288
00:16:32,920 --> 00:16:35,077
I assure you, nothing
good can come of this!

289
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:36,689
Yeah, my thoughts exactly!

290
00:16:44,820 --> 00:16:48,860
You have made me so proud of
you, Smiley, until we meet again.

291
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:16,100
Now, be reborn and arise.

292
00:17:16,800 --> 00:17:20,120
Become the ultimate
weapon, land of the dead.

293
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:25,080
Transform this island
into a lethal wasteland.

294
00:17:52,220 --> 00:17:54,060
What's wrong with my legs?

295
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:56,300
What's it doing to me?

296
00:18:01,860 --> 00:18:03,920
Someone help me!

297
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:13,630
Ahh!

298
00:18:13,713 --> 00:18:14,543
It's poison gas!

299
00:18:14,626 --> 00:18:15,456
Keep running!

300
00:18:15,539 --> 00:18:16,413
Don't let it touch you!

301
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:24,360
I can't move my body!

302
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:27,060
It's like a statue!

303
00:18:30,620 --> 00:18:31,800
Oh no! Oh no!

304
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:33,800
It's getting on us! Master!

305
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:41,900
Yes, the experiment is a success!

306
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:44,755
I have perfected an inescapable death.

307
00:18:44,980 --> 00:18:46,900
No one walks away from this.

308
00:18:47,720 --> 00:18:52,297
Although the poison from my last experiment
worked, there were still survivors.

309
00:18:52,380 --> 00:18:55,780
They were ambulatory,
able to seek medical aid.

310
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:57,335
That was the problem.

311
00:18:57,600 --> 00:19:00,340
I should have immobilized
them from the start.

312
00:19:00,740 --> 00:19:04,100
This new gas smothers the
body in a shell like ash.

313
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:09,460
The toxins seep through the skin
and instantly paralyze the victim.

314
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:18,077
Behold the most effective
mass-manufactured massacre spread

315
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:22,220
my toxic death show this world
what a living hell looks like

316
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:37,380
This is pure madness

317
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:43,390
No!

318
00:19:43,473 --> 00:19:44,600
I want to live!

319
00:19:46,780 --> 00:19:48,400
They're freezing solid!

320
00:19:56,800 --> 00:19:58,540
Hey, what is this crap?

321
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:00,897
It's like some kind of horror show.

322
00:20:00,980 --> 00:20:05,157
All the ones that got wiped out, they
look like Caesar's freak show soldiers.

323
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:08,240
I'm just glad we're not
where that purple smoke is.

324
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:10,395
Actually, wait a sec.

325
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:11,637
Where do you think they're filming this?

326
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:15,340
I wonder, don't turn around
if you haven't figured it out.

327
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:29,637
No, that massacre happened
right behind us—help, master!

328
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:30,550
master

329
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:39,060
Oh crap if that stuff touches us,
we'll end up like them. We're doomed.

330
00:20:39,220 --> 00:20:42,377
We're on an island We can't
outrun a cloud of death gas now,

331
00:20:42,460 --> 00:20:45,797
I get it—they sealed up the lab so they
can keep the gas from getting inside.

332
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:52,357
Open the damn door, Caesar,
you heartless bastard!

333
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:54,397
I don't want to die on your Frozen Island.

334
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:57,817
Damn, damn it, damn you—let us in!

335
00:20:57,900 --> 00:20:58,730
Crap, it's

336
00:21:15,760 --> 00:21:17,617
about to catch up to us?

337
00:21:17,700 --> 00:21:18,530
to us

338
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:22,437
If you fall behind,
we'll have to leave you!

339
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:24,696
Slow down and you're as good as dead!

340
00:21:30,300 --> 00:21:31,130
Dino!

341
00:21:31,213 --> 00:21:33,280
There's no way we can outrun it!

342
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:41,417
There's some kind of
large animal up ahead!

343
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:43,206
It looks like a giant lizard!

344
00:21:44,220 --> 00:21:45,100
No, it's...

345
00:21:48,580 --> 00:21:53,157
It's a dragon, a dragon, so it would
appear—don't give me that crap!

346
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:54,517
Dragons are from fairy tales.

347
00:21:54,600 --> 00:21:56,137
They're real enough on this island,

348
00:21:56,220 --> 00:21:58,737
but this one looks smaller
than the other one I saw.

349
00:21:58,820 --> 00:22:01,357
Holy crap—we can fly on the damn thing!

350
00:22:01,440 --> 00:22:05,457
If we catch it, that's a brilliant
idea—then let's do it and do it fast.

351
00:22:05,540 --> 00:22:08,337
I can't keep running like this—wait
up, you fairy tale bastard!

352
00:22:08,420 --> 00:22:09,780
you fairy tale bastard

353
00:22:16,960 --> 00:22:18,060
Hey, that's Zoro!

354
00:22:18,340 --> 00:22:20,399
They're all running from the smoke!

355
00:22:22,300 --> 00:22:23,997
Would you look at those fools?

356
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:25,397
What are they doing out there?

357
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:28,037
And what the hell kind
of stupid run is that?

358
00:22:28,120 --> 00:22:30,826
Oh, look, the samurai
got his whole body back.

359
00:22:31,700 --> 00:22:32,880
Yeah, you're right!

360
00:22:33,120 --> 00:22:35,397
Guess that means he's not
gonna give me his legs.

361
00:22:35,480 --> 00:22:38,362
Hey, wait, that's not
important right now, Robin!

362
00:22:39,080 --> 00:22:40,420
Run faster, guys!

363
00:22:40,620 --> 00:22:42,177
That smoke will freeze you dead!

364
00:22:42,260 --> 00:22:43,100
You gotta run!

365
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:47,120
Oh, man.

366
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:49,377
I don't have the strength to yell.

367
00:22:49,460 --> 00:22:50,290
Damn it.

368
00:22:50,373 --> 00:22:51,760
Don't see Prism Stone.

369
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:56,176
I take it those are friends
of yours, Straw Hat Luffy.

370
00:22:58,280 --> 00:23:02,104
Well, that does help to explain
why they're so difficult to kill.

371
00:23:04,020 --> 00:23:07,902
But their lungs will soon give out
and the gas will overtake them.

372
00:23:10,980 --> 00:23:17,000
In a mere matter of minutes now, this
island will truly become a land of the dead.

373
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:22,260
Nothing can survive
outside of these walls.

374
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:25,420
Not one single soul will be left alive.

375
00:23:29,780 --> 00:23:33,040
Oh, by the way, that includes you too.

376
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:36,680
What's happening?

377
00:23:50,360 --> 00:23:54,017
and now I offer you all
as proof to the world:

378
00:23:54,100 --> 00:23:57,357
evidence of the true
destructive power of my land.

379
00:23:57,440 --> 00:24:00,797
of the Dead: a pirate
with 400 million berries,

380
00:24:00,880 --> 00:24:06,860
a vice admiral of the navy, and
even a dreaded Warlord of the sea.

381
00:24:07,740 --> 00:24:09,597
You're all completely helpless.

382
00:24:09,680 --> 00:24:12,720
Against my genius tide of death!

383
00:24:16,700 --> 00:24:17,530
What

384
00:24:17,613 --> 00:24:23,780
do I do?

385
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:24,790
Think!

386
00:24:24,873 --> 00:24:27,837
I've gotta do something or
he's gonna kill all my friends!

387
00:24:27,920 --> 00:24:29,600
But how can I help?

388
00:24:29,780 --> 00:24:32,657
With these injuries, I'll
only get myself captured!

389
00:24:32,740 --> 00:24:36,860
And if that happens, the drug
formula and sedatives I found,

390
00:24:37,100 --> 00:24:38,660
it'll all be for nothing!

391
00:24:39,620 --> 00:24:40,480
Oh no!

392
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:42,586
I just don't know what to do!

393
00:24:49,620 --> 00:24:52,420
I really don't need any
more close calls today!

394
00:24:52,920 --> 00:24:54,480
Wait, what is this?

395
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:58,520
Don't do anything.

396
00:24:59,440 --> 00:25:00,558
Who's through this?

397
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:05,860
Whoa, look who's inside!

398
00:25:06,180 --> 00:25:07,337
It's Smokey!

399
00:25:07,420 --> 00:25:08,260
It's Tashigi!

400
00:25:08,360 --> 00:25:10,301
My goodness, they're still alive!

401
00:25:10,760 --> 00:25:11,840
Uh, hang on.

402
00:25:12,100 --> 00:25:14,480
They're all wrapped in chains! Damn it!

403
00:25:14,660 --> 00:25:17,960
We really are all gonna
die! Smokey! That's Shoujou!

404
00:25:18,940 --> 00:25:19,770
Guys!

405
00:25:30,300 --> 00:25:32,037
They really built that lab.

406
00:25:32,120 --> 00:25:35,917
As solid as a fortress, very true,

407
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:40,397
and rather well designed for
maneuvering heavy equipment.

408
00:25:40,480 --> 00:25:43,737
How can you two be so relaxed?

409
00:25:43,820 --> 00:25:47,477
How are we getting out of this jam?

410
00:25:47,560 --> 00:25:52,800
I wasn't expecting Vergo
to show up, but no matter.

411
00:25:54,820 --> 00:25:58,537
I'm not gonna let a small detail like
that hold us back now, Straw Hat—we're...

412
00:25:58,620 --> 00:25:59,960
we're

413
00:26:02,740 --> 00:26:03,717
sticking with the plan.

414
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:05,377
Just don't screw it up again.

415
00:26:05,460 --> 00:26:07,107
Time for the counter-attack.
